# Memory Rules

- Prefer RAII everywhere.
- Avoid raw new/delete.
- Prefer std::unique_ptr for ownership.
- Use std::shared_ptr only when ownership is truly shared.
- Prefer stack allocation when practical.
- Minimize heap allocations in hot paths.
- Avoid memory leaks.
- Avoid hidden ownership transfer.
- Prefer move semantics where appropriate.
- Keep ownership semantics explicit.
- Avoid unnecessary copies.